cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ECGrav in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: ECGrav
abstract: >-
  A Wolfram Language paclet for studying models in which geometry — and
  ultimately gravity — emerges from the statistical mechanics of combinatorial
  structures (graphs and simplicial complexes). It provides tools for the
  combinatorics and topology of pure simplicial complexes and their graphs, and
  a Monte Carlo statistical-mechanics toolkit (Metropolis, parallel tempering,
  multi-histogram reweighting, and exact enumeration) over energy functionals
  that reward manifold-like configurations.
type: software
